Design a thermal management block that monitors a temperature signal to control fan speed. It generates a fan control signal and a feedback signal based on incoming temperature readings. The module ensures that when the temperature is within a safe range (between 30 and 70 degrees), a 'safe' state is maintained. If the temperature exceeds 70 degrees, the fan speed increases, while a temperature drop below 30 degrees decreases the fan speed. The module employs basic logic to adjust fan operation dynamically, ensuring efficient cooling in response to thermal changes.
