description:
Design a 4-bit delay line circuit that captures an input signal A on the rising edge of the clock and outputs a delayed version as X. The output X reflects the value of A from two clock cycles prior, effectively introducing a two-cycle delay. This circuit utilizes two internal registers to store the delayed values.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input clk,
    output reg [3:0] X
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input clk,
    output reg [3:0] X
);reg [3:0] delayed_A;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    delayed_A <= A;
    X <= delayed_A;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    delayed_A <= X;
end

endmodule

