description:
Design a 3-to-8 decoder that generates an 8-bit output, `y`, based on a 3-bit input, `x`. Each bit of the output `y` corresponds to one of the possible combinations of the input signals, where only one bit will be high (logic '1') corresponding to the binary value of `x`, while all others will be low (logic '0'). Additionally, the module includes a second output, `z`, which produces a one-hot encoded signal representing the same value as `x`, but shifted to the left, providing another representation of the selected output line.
