Design a clock generator that produces a clock signal with a frequency determined by a counter. The module increments a 32-bit counter on each positive edge of the generated clock signal. When the counter reaches a value of 125, the output clock signal toggles to high; otherwise, it is low. This creates a clock signal with a specific period based on the counter's threshold, which can be adjusted by modifying the threshold value.
module top_module(
  output reg clk
);

